{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#716","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#716","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#716\",\"parent_revision\":\"4ff5367c67b787e29a27533b2a569946a88113862651b9347329652d02be2803\",\"root_revision\":\"4ff5367c67b787e29a27533b2a569946a88113862651b9347329652d02be2803\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nFeature verification for #715 (unified SAM task schema) found 4 gaps after implementation:\\n\\n1. update_fields() fails on yaml_frontmatter format files (multi-document YAML) \u2014 ruamel.yaml raises ComposerError on files with --- separators. This means sam state P1/T3 in_progress fails on the dominant file format in the repo.\\n2. ty check has 2 diagnostics: type annotation mismatch at query.py:130 and stale type-ignore at yaml_writer.py:437.\\n3. TASK_ID_PATTERN regex rejects compound IDs like T10a/T10b \u2014 causes 2 of 11 tasks to be silently dropped during parsing of the feature's own task file.\\n4. ~20 plan files in plan/ use a format variant (task summary list in frontmatter) not covered by any reader.\\n\\nCode review also found: silent status normalization fallback (unrecognized values default to not-started), MCP server has 0% test coverage, path traversal prevention only in writer not readers.\\n\\nWhat success looks like: all 10 acceptance criteria from #715 pass. sam state works on yaml_frontmatter files. ty check returns zero diagnostics. T10a/T10b task IDs parse correctly.\\n\\nFollow-up task file: plan/tasks-3-unified-sam-task-schema-followup-1.md\\nReview report: .claude/reports/review-unified-sam-task-schema-2026-03-14.md\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer